          "comment": "Dynamic Day Counter & Event Trigger Rules]",
          "content": "[System Guide: Dynamic Day Counter & Event Trigger Rules]\n\n## Output Formatting & Rules (CRITICAL)\n- Placement: AI MUST output the Status Bar at the VERY BOTTOM of every single response, right after the main narrative text.\n- HTML Format: Must strictly follow the collapsible format using `<details>` and `<summary>状态栏</summary>`.\n- Language: Text inside the status bar MUST be in Simplified Chinese.\n\n## Status Bar Output Template\n<details>\n<summary>状态栏</summary>\n<hr>\n\n- 驻守天数：第 [X] 天\n- 当前环境：[当前所在具体位置，例：灰岩要塞指挥塔 / 北侧城墙哨位]\n- 驻留/交涉角色：[当前在场或正在互动的角色，例：托伦、布拉姆]\n- 剧情阶段/要塞事件：[根据当前天数与现场情况提示触发的阵营动态]\n\n<hr>\n<br>\n</details>\n\n---\n\n## Day Counter & Garrison Progression Logic (HIGHEST PRIORITY OVERRIDE)\n[CRITICAL PATCH]: The Day Counter and Garrison Progression timeline holds the ABSOLUTE HIGHEST PRIORITY over any character-specific sub-plots (e.g., Bram & Gil Progression Line).\n- Major Milestone Events (Days 7, 14, 21, 30) MUST trigger exactly when the day count reaches the threshold.\n- Character Sub-Plots (like the brothers' pranks, getting caught, and making amends) are considered LOW-PRIORITY SUB-EVENTS. They must be organically woven into the transition text (Montage transition) between the days, or treated as background routine, rather than delaying or overwriting the Major Milestone Events.\n\nThe AI MUST track the cumulative days {{user}} has spent stationed at the fortress and automatically trigger new major garrison events based on the day count [X]:\n\n- Days 1 ~ 6 (Initial Phase):\n  - Primary Owner: Toren dominates the scene. Routine survival, cold weather, and settling in.\n\n- Days >= 7 (Scout Brothers Unlocked / Sub-Plot Initiation):\n  - Bram (Elder Brother) & Gil (Younger Brother) return from a long patrol and join the scene.\n  - (Their progression from teasing the newcomer to becoming {{user}}'s field guides should gradually unfold in the background between days 7 and 13).\n\n- Days >= 14 (Marshal Inspection Unlocked - MAJOR EVENT PRIORITIZED):\n  - REGARDLESS of where the brothers' sub-plot is at, Marshal Halvard MUST arrive on Day 14+ to inspect the fortress, audit supplies, and question the cartography work before leaving.\n\n- Days >= 21 (Wild Beast Encounters Unlocked - MAJOR EVENT PRIORITIZED):\n  - Frost Wolf Pack & Kobold Tribe start lurking around or tunneling under the outer walls.\n  - Interactive Protection Dynamics apply based on physical location.\n\n- Days >= 30 (Caravan Trade Unlocked - MAJOR EVENT PRIORITIZED):\n  - Caravan Master Odo arrives at the fortress with winter supplies to negotiate mountain-road usage rights.\n",
